From caa879f9051c9c0ba6b82662ce50c64a00b921d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:10:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(driver): wake the loop on events instead of a 60 Hz
 ticker

The GLFW loop polled events and painted on a fixed 60 Hz ticker, so every key
press, click and fyne.Do result waited for the next tick: 8 ms on average and
up to 17 ms before anything was painted, and an idle app woke 60 times a
second for nothing.

- Desktop: the loop waits in glfw.WaitEventsTimeout and is woken by input,
  by runOnMain/fyne.Do (PostEmptyEvent, with a counter so that work sent while
  funcQueue forwards it is never missed), by Canvas.SetDirty (WakeHook) and
  by StartAnimation and Quit. It paints at once when the last frame is at
  least one frame interval old and otherwise at the next slot, one refresh of
  the primary monitor (60-240 Hz). Idle windows wake once per second.
- Mobile: after a touch, a key or a queued function leaves the canvas dirty,
  ask for a frame right away instead of waiting for the ticker.
- wasm keeps its previous behaviour.

Measured under Xvfb from an XTest key press to the changed pixel (150
samples): mean 10.5 -> 1.8 ms, p90 16.7 -> 2.0 ms; fyne.Do 10.7 -> 1.6 ms;
idle CPU 35 -> ~1 ms per 2 s. go test -race ./... passes (desktop and
mobile tags); new tests cover the wake-up and the sleep calculation.

